# Trivy Ignore File for Audio Processor
# This file documents vulnerabilities that are accepted risks or cannot be fixed yet.
# Each entry should have a clear justification.

# CVE-2025-13601 - libglib2.0-0t64 heap buffer overflow in g_escape_uri_string()
# Status: No fix available in Debian as of 2025-12-06
# Severity: HIGH
# Risk Assessment: LOW for this application
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability requires calling g_escape_uri_string() with a very large number
#     of unacceptable characters that need escaping
#   - This application does not use GLib URI escaping functionality
#   - Upstream patches exist (glib 2.86.2) but not yet backported to Debian
#   - Tracking: Debian bug #1121488
# References:
#   - https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-13601
#   - https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/issues/3827
#   - https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4914
# Review Date: 2025-12-06
# Next Review: When Debian releases patch (monitor bug #1121488)
CVE-2025-13601

# CVE-2025-64720, CVE-2025-65018, CVE-2025-66293 - libpng16-16t64 vulnerabilities
# Status: No fix available in Debian 13.2 as of 2025-12-06
# Severity: HIGH (all three)
# Risk Assessment: LOW for this application
# Justification:
#   - CVE-2025-64720: Buffer overflow in png_image_read_composite
#   - CVE-2025-65018: Heap buffer overflow in libpng
#   - CVE-2025-66293: Out-of-bounds read in png_image_read_composite
#   - Application uses libpng only through Python libraries (Pillow, matplotlib)
#   - No direct manipulation of PNG internals or untrusted PNG files in processing pipeline
#   - Debian security tracker shows "affected" status with no fix version yet
# References:
#   - https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-64720
#   - https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-65018
#   - https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-66293
# Review Date: 2025-12-06
# Next Review: When Debian releases patched version
CVE-2025-64720
CVE-2025-65018
CVE-2025-66293

# CVE-2026-40393 - libgbm1 / mesa-libgallium (Mesa GBM / Gallium)
# Status: will_not_fix (Debian security tracker)
# Severity: CRITICAL
# Risk Assessment: NEGLIGIBLE for this application
# Justification:
#   - Vulnerability is in Mesa's hardware-accelerated graphics buffer
#     management (GBM) and Gallium driver layer
#   - This is a server-side audio processing service: no display server,
#     no GPU access, no graphics rendering, headless container
#   - libgbm1 / mesa-libgallium are pulled in only as transitive deps of
#     libavcodec-extra (ffmpeg) for hardware video acceleration codepaths
#     that this application never exercises
#   - Container runs as non-root user with no /dev/dri access
# References:
#   - https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-40393
# Review Date: 2026-05-18
# Next Review: 2026-07-17 (60-day cap per CLAUDE.md unfixed-CVE policy)
CVE-2026-40393

# CVE-2026-33846 - gnutls28 (GnuTLS)
# Status: No upstream fix available
# Severity: HIGH
# Risk Assessment: LOW for this application
# Justification:
#   - GnuTLS is a transitive dependency of curl and ffmpeg in the base
#     image, used only for command-line TLS in CI tooling
#   - Application Python code uses OpenSSL (via cryptography / urllib3),
#     not GnuTLS, for outbound TLS
#   - No untrusted TLS server certificates are processed by GnuTLS in this
#     application's request path
#   - Upstream GnuTLS has not yet published a fixed release; Debian
#     security tracker shows no fix candidate
# References:
#   - https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-33846
# Review Date: 2026-05-18
# Next Review: 2026-07-17 (60-day cap per CLAUDE.md unfixed-CVE policy)
CVE-2026-33846

# CVE-2026-5673 - libtheoradec1 (Theora video decoder)
# Status: fix_deferred (Debian security tracker)
# Severity: HIGH
# Risk Assessment: NEGLIGIBLE for this application
# Justification:
#   - libtheoradec1 decodes Ogg Theora video streams
#   - This is an audio processing service; it does not decode video
#   - libtheoradec1 is pulled in transitively by libavcodec-extra (ffmpeg)
#     for completeness of codec support, but the application never invokes
#     Theora decoding via ffmpeg
#   - Debian has classified this as fix_deferred, meaning low-impact in
#     typical Debian deployments
# References:
#   - https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-5673
# Review Date: 2026-05-18
# Next Review: 2026-07-17 (60-day cap per CLAUDE.md unfixed-CVE policy)
CVE-2026-5673
